<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=turtle-ship">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Weapons and war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turtle ship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1413</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as geobukseon, gwiseon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The turtle ship (geobukseon) was a Korean warship named after its covering, said to resemble a turtle's shell, and first recorded in 1413 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/annals-of-the-joseon-dynasty">Annals of the Joseon Dynasty</a>. Its roof was covered with iron spikes against boarding, it was driven by both oars and sails, and it carried several types of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> and a dragon's head at the bow. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yi-sun-sin">Admiral Yi</a> Sun-sin, credited with designing an improved version, used turtle ships against the Japanese invasions of 1592–1598; whether they were armoured with iron plates is disputed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/turtle-ship.jpg" alt="Turtle ship" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: From the Yi Chungmugong Jeonseo (1795); National Diet Library · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geobukseon1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1413</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Korea</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/empire/joseon">Joseon</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Admiral Yi Sun-sin used an improved design against the Japanese invasions of 1592–1598; whether it was armoured with iron plates is disputed.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/cannon">Cannon<span>by 1288</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=turtle-ship">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
